	Please do following before using software:

* In your AUTOEXEC.BAT file, add the installation directory to your path.
   If you installed to C:\COP, and your path currently is:
   PATH=C:\ 
   Change it to:
   PATH=C:\COP;C:\

* In your AUTOEXEC.BAT file, add the following:
  SET COP=C:\COP   (assuming C:\COP is your installation directory)

* In your CONFIG.SYS file, the following should specify 16 or more:
   FILES=16

* For performance improvement, install a disk cache and RAM disk; 
  for example, see DOS/MS-Windows manual to install SMARTDRV.SYS and
  RAMDRIVE.SYS in your CONFIG.SYS file. Recommended disk cache size and 
  recommended RAM disk size is 256K or larger. If memory is limited, 
  disk cache generally provides more improvement than RAM disk. 
  If RAM disk is installed, add the following to your AUTOEXEC.BAT file,
   MKDIR G:\TMP     	(if G: is your RAM drive)
   SET TMP=G:\tmp
  This will direct temporary files to RAM disk, which improves link time.

* Read printed release letter (or file ASMREL.LET in installation directory).
